1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,700
As far as I can remember, I’ve always been a night owl.
从我记事起，我就一直是个夜猫子。

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,940
Even in middle school I would stay up very late.
早在上中学时，我就常常熬到很晚。

3
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:13,270
I would feel completely at ease doing my homework in bed, with light music on.
开着轻音乐、躺在床上写作业，我会觉得无比自在。

4
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:20,380
I found comfort in keeping myself awake when everyone else had gone to bed, and I loved the silence of the night.
别人都睡了，我却让自己醒着，从中得到慰藉；我也爱夜晚的寂静。

5
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:27,220
My parents urged me to get out of this so-called unhealthy habit, but their repeated requests fell on deaf ears.
父母催我改掉这个所谓的不健康习惯，可他们一再的要求我全当耳旁风。

6
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:30,140
Fast forward to my first year of college.
时间快进到我上大学的第一年。

7
00:00:30,940 --> 00:00:37,980
I still loved the night and would stay up until ungodly hours for no apparent reason, chatting online and watching videos.
我依然爱着夜晚，常常毫无来由地熬到深更半夜，在网上聊天、看视频。

8
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:44,210
When I finally started to study, I would race through the assigned work, often well past midnight.
等终于开始学习时，我常常匆匆赶完布置的作业，往往一直写到半夜过后很久。

9
00:00:45,010 --> 00:00:49,930
My roommates would tell me to go to bed and get up early the following morning to do it instead.
室友们会劝我上床睡觉，第二天早上早起再写。

10
00:00:50,730 --> 00:00:52,360
Get up early to do my homework?
早起写作业？

11
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:53,870
No way!
不可能！

12
00:00:54,670 --> 00:00:55,970
I would never do that.
我绝不会那样做。

13
00:00:56,770 --> 00:00:59,810
Then, one day last term, I did exactly that.
后来，上学期的一天，我恰恰就这么做了。

14
00:01:00,610 --> 00:01:07,620
Bent over my laptop while sitting on the bed in the corner of my room, I suddenly felt a pounding headache, and had to lie down.
我坐在房间角落的床上，伏在笔记本电脑前，突然一阵剧烈的头痛袭来，只好躺下。

15
00:01:08,420 --> 00:01:14,360
Unable to keep my eyes open, I decided I had no choice but to finish my homework the next morning.
我困得睁不开眼，觉得别无选择，只能第二天早上再把作业写完。

16
00:01:15,160 --> 00:01:16,530
I woke up at 6am.
我早上六点就醒了。

17
00:01:17,330 --> 00:01:21,240
Hardly had I written half a page when I felt a sharp pain in my chest.
我刚写了半页，胸口就一阵剧痛。

18
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:28,630
At the school clinic, a doctor, with a serious expression on his face, handed me a medical report.
在校医务室，一位医生神情严肃地递给我一份体检报告。

19
00:01:29,430 --> 00:01:32,230
“You’re 20, but your heart is 40!” he said.
“你才二十岁，心脏却已经四十岁了！”他说。

20
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:34,510
A cold wave went through me.
我浑身一阵发凉。

21
00:01:35,310 --> 00:01:41,170
I realized that years of living as a late-night person had turned my heart into an overworked engine.
我意识到，多年来当夜猫子，已经把我的心脏变成了一台超负荷运转的引擎。

22
00:01:41,970 --> 00:01:45,390
Struck by the doctor’s warning, I knew I had to make a change.
医生的警告让我深受触动，我知道自己必须做出改变。

23
00:01:46,190 --> 00:01:50,250
Slowly but surely, my efforts to adjust to the new routine paid off.
慢慢地、却也确确实实地，我为适应新作息所做的努力有了回报。
